ROOT CAUSE, read from the source (hooks/refresh.mjs:92):
  const tmp = real(os.tmpdir());
  node -e os.tmpdir() on this machine = /var/folders/5b/.../T
  So the tmp arm covers ONLY $TMPDIR. /tmp and /private/tmp - the classic
  scratch directories, and ones macOS periodic actually sweeps - are NOT covered.
SECOND, LATENT: notDurable(p) takes a candidate path `p`, but its worktree arm
  tests fs.statSync(path.join(PKG_DIR, '.git')) - PKG_DIR, the RUNNING module's
  directory, not `p`. Today they coincide because GATE_BIN is a sibling; the
  parameter is nonetheless ignored. NOT a live defect, recorded as latent.

